{"data":{"featured":{"edges":[{"node":{"frontmatter":{"title":"OpenClimateFix Weather Pipeline","cover":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"constrained","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/34fee15acf4df41caa09742bde0f5cb6/7721e/cover.jpg","srcSet":"/static/34fee15acf4df41caa09742bde0f5cb6/d67e7/cover.jpg 175w,\n/static/34fee15acf4df41caa09742bde0f5cb6/9fb4e/cover.jpg 350w,\n/static/34fee15acf4df41caa09742bde0f5cb6/7721e/cover.jpg 700w,\n/static/34fee15acf4df41caa09742bde0f5cb6/8e1e8/cover.jpg 1400w","sizes":"(min-width: 700px) 700px, 100vw"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/34fee15acf4df41caa09742bde0f5cb6/9aa63/cover.avif 175w,\n/static/34fee15acf4df41caa09742bde0f5cb6/e6db6/cover.avif 350w,\n/static/34fee15acf4df41caa09742bde0f5cb6/f47db/cover.avif 700w,\n/static/34fee15acf4df41caa09742bde0f5cb6/8fee6/cover.avif 1400w","type":"image/avif","sizes":"(min-width: 700px) 700px, 100vw"},{"srcSet":"/static/34fee15acf4df41caa09742bde0f5cb6/240e7/cover.webp 175w,\n/static/34fee15acf4df41caa09742bde0f5cb6/faefe/cover.webp 350w,\n/static/34fee15acf4df41caa09742bde0f5cb6/d5dc4/cover.webp 700w,\n/static/34fee15acf4df41caa09742bde0f5cb6/e2f1a/cover.webp 1400w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"(min-width: 700px) 700px, 100vw"}]},"width":700,"height":438}}},"tech":["Python","Apache Airflow","PyTorch","Graph Neural Networks","Apache Kafka"],"github":"https://github.com/openclimatefix","external":"https://openclimatefix.org/","cta":""},"html":"<p>Solar forecasts decide how much gas a grid operator burns as backup. OpenClimateFix makes those forecasts better, in the open, and I work on their weather models.</p>\n<p>Validation pipelines in Airflow so bad sensor data never reaches training. Anomaly detection for readings that look wrong. Distributed-training tweaks so the GNNs are cheaper to retrain. Unglamorous, useful.</p>"}},{"node":{"frontmatter":{"title":"AI Ticket Triage, Fully Local","cover":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"constrained","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/c8ad7413b4d03d0e91af08c5b2d23daf/d2194/cover.png","srcSet":"/static/c8ad7413b4d03d0e91af08c5b2d23daf/cebcc/cover.png 175w,\n/static/c8ad7413b4d03d0e91af08c5b2d23daf/272cf/cover.png 350w,\n/static/c8ad7413b4d03d0e91af08c5b2d23daf/d2194/cover.png 700w,\n/static/c8ad7413b4d03d0e91af08c5b2d23daf/b50c4/cover.png 1400w","sizes":"(min-width: 700px) 700px, 100vw"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/c8ad7413b4d03d0e91af08c5b2d23daf/9aa63/cover.avif 175w,\n/static/c8ad7413b4d03d0e91af08c5b2d23daf/e6db6/cover.avif 350w,\n/static/c8ad7413b4d03d0e91af08c5b2d23daf/f47db/cover.avif 700w,\n/static/c8ad7413b4d03d0e91af08c5b2d23daf/8fee6/cover.avif 1400w","type":"image/avif","sizes":"(min-width: 700px) 700px, 100vw"},{"srcSet":"/static/c8ad7413b4d03d0e91af08c5b2d23daf/240e7/cover.webp 175w,\n/static/c8ad7413b4d03d0e91af08c5b2d23daf/faefe/cover.webp 350w,\n/static/c8ad7413b4d03d0e91af08c5b2d23daf/d5dc4/cover.webp 700w,\n/static/c8ad7413b4d03d0e91af08c5b2d23daf/e2f1a/cover.webp 1400w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"(min-width: 700px) 700px, 100vw"}]},"width":700,"height":438}}},"tech":["LangGraph","Ollama","Qwen3","FastAPI","LangSmith"],"github":"https://github.com/glitch401/p1-seafoam-cicada","external":"https://github.com/glitch401/p1-seafoam-cicada","cta":""},"html":"<p>Support queues die by a thousand lookups. Find the order, check the policy, draft the reply. This agent does the boring parts, and it never sends a byte to the cloud.</p>\n<p>LangGraph keeps state in sticky threads pinned to Order IDs, Qwen3 runs on my own hardware through Ollama, and LangSmith traces every step so I can see why the agent wrote what it wrote. There's a Next.js chat UI on top.</p>"}},{"node":{"frontmatter":{"title":"Three.js Experiments (2018)","cover":{"childImageSharp":{"gatsbyImageData":{"layout":"constrained","placeholder":{"fallback":"data:image/png;base64,"},"images":{"fallback":{"src":"/static/ea7de78342d48c3dea8907635363ef5e/d2194/cover.png","srcSet":"/static/ea7de78342d48c3dea8907635363ef5e/cebcc/cover.png 175w,\n/static/ea7de78342d48c3dea8907635363ef5e/272cf/cover.png 350w,\n/static/ea7de78342d48c3dea8907635363ef5e/d2194/cover.png 700w,\n/static/ea7de78342d48c3dea8907635363ef5e/b50c4/cover.png 1400w","sizes":"(min-width: 700px) 700px, 100vw"},"sources":[{"srcSet":"/static/ea7de78342d48c3dea8907635363ef5e/9aa63/cover.avif 175w,\n/static/ea7de78342d48c3dea8907635363ef5e/e6db6/cover.avif 350w,\n/static/ea7de78342d48c3dea8907635363ef5e/f47db/cover.avif 700w,\n/static/ea7de78342d48c3dea8907635363ef5e/8fee6/cover.avif 1400w","type":"image/avif","sizes":"(min-width: 700px) 700px, 100vw"},{"srcSet":"/static/ea7de78342d48c3dea8907635363ef5e/240e7/cover.webp 175w,\n/static/ea7de78342d48c3dea8907635363ef5e/faefe/cover.webp 350w,\n/static/ea7de78342d48c3dea8907635363ef5e/d5dc4/cover.webp 700w,\n/static/ea7de78342d48c3dea8907635363ef5e/e2f1a/cover.webp 1400w","type":"image/webp","sizes":"(min-width: 700px) 700px, 100vw"}]},"width":700,"height":438}}},"tech":["Three.js","WebGL","JavaScript"],"github":"https://github.com/glitch401/threejs_experiments","external":"https://glitch401.github.io/threejs_experiments/","cta":"https://glitch401.github.io/threejs_experiments/"},"html":"<p>Before the graphs and the language models there was this: a pile of little Three.js experiments I built for an internship task at IIT Bombay, back in 2018. Spinning geometry, particles, my first camera controls.</p>\n<p>They're still online, preserved exactly as they were, bugs included. Go click around.</p>"}}]}}}